## Language-Specific Patterns

### For TypeScript/JavaScript (Playwright/Cypress)
- Use async/await patterns
- Implement Page Object Model when complex
- Use Playwright's built-in assertions
- Enable trace/screenshot artifacts

### For Python (Pytest/Playwright)
- Use fixtures for setup/teardown
- Implement page objects as classes
- Use pytest parametrize for data-driven tests
- Enable pytest-html for reporting

### For C# (NUnit/xUnit)
- Use [SetUp] and [TearDown] attributes
- Implement IDisposable for cleanup
- Use async Task methods for async operations
- Enable NUnit test reporting

### For Java (JUnit/TestNG)
- Use @BeforeEach/@AfterEach annotations
- Implement AutoCloseable for resources
- Use AssertJ for fluent assertions
- Enable Allure reporting

### For Ruby (RSpec/Capybara)
- Use before/after hooks
- Implement helper modules
- Use expect syntax for assertions
- Enable RSpec HTML formatter

